From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:06:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 134/260] [ae-patch] Show the effort a Claude session runs at
 and lay the model menu out as one column

The composer's model menu said "Effort: Claude default" whenever no effort was
pinned, and the chip under the composer named only the model. Both now show the
level the session actually runs at: the settings-file level the runner
recorded, else Claude Code's own default for the model, read from the model
catalog in its binary (Opus 5.5 medium, Fable 5.1 high, Sonnet 5.5 medium).
Claude sessions use Claude Code's words, "Extra" for xhigh, so the chip reads
"Fable 5.1 1M High" like desktop Claude Code's "Opus 5.5 Extra".

The menu is one column like desktop's: an Account row whose submenu lists the
host's logins and the shared ones, the models as numbered rows a digit can
pick, "Effort" with the level right-aligned and the default tagged in its
submenu, Previous models, and a one-line Fast mode toggle whose unsupported-
model reason is the row's tooltip.
